\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A declared basis recovers the paired Dirac matrix}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{In any chosen orthonormal basis of #{\mathcal H} from
\ref{fdip-009O}, the [paired Grassmann formula](fdip-008H) applies
to #{mI+D_U} of \ref{fdip-009P} as a finite complex matrix. The
basis map is the coordinate isomorphism determined by that ordered
frame. This observation requires neither positivity nor
invertibility and is not an ordinary probability interpretation.}
